<title>USA: US FCC backs transfer of PanAmSat control.</title>
<headline>US FCC backs transfer of PanAmSat control.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Federal Communications Commission said Friday that it approved the transfer of control of PanAmSat Corp to a unit of Hughes Electronics Corp.</p>
<p>Hughes and PanAmSat announced last September that they would merge their satellite services operations, pending necessary approvals.</p>
<p>In granting the transfer, the FCC said the deal &quot;will serve the public interest by enhancing competition in the satellite services market, both domestically and internationally.&quot;</p>
</text>
